    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In this section, to get insight to the theoretical findings of the previous sections, we present a set of numerical results that compare the symbol error rates (SERs) of the quasiorthogonal and quasi-biorthogonal signaling methods against their respective orthogonal and biorthogonal counterparts. The goal here is to explore the amount of performance loss incurred as the non-orthogonality of the symbol vectors increases. Also, through numerical results, we examine the tightness of the upper bounds that were derived in Section V. Here, to generate a set of non-orthogonal codes, we begin"
